Package: com.ayugram.pushrelay
Name: AyuGram Push Relay
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
Maintainer: AyuGram Build <build@ayugram.local>
Author: AyuGram Build
Section: Tweak Injection
Priority: optional
Description: Relay APNs push from an app that already receives it (App Store
 Swiftgram or official Telegram) into AyuGram, over a Darwin notification.
 AyuGram then catches up with the server via a forced getDifference, so chats,
 counters and message history stay current while it is alive in the background.
 .
 The tweak hooks application:didReceiveRemoteNotification:fetchCompletionHandler:
 and pushRegistry:didReceiveIncomingPushWith:for:completion: and posts the
 Darwin notification com.ayugram.push.signal. It never breaks the host app:
 the original methods are called unchanged.
 .
 The dylib uses no Substrate or ElleKit symbols - only the Objective-C runtime -
 so it works with any tweak loader that scans MobileSubstrate/DynamicLibraries
 (ElleKit, Substitute, libhooker).
 .
 After install, edit
 /var/jb/Library/MobileSubstrate/DynamicLibraries/AyuGramPushRelay.plist
 and put the bundle id of the host app into the Bundles array.
